# MyFamily Hub — always-on project rule

## Before coding
- Read `10_docs/작업내용.md` for current status and next priorities.
- Follow product requirements in `10_docs/기획서.md` / `10_docs/프롬프트.md`.
- Respect folder layout: `20_client`, `40_server`, `30_data`, `10_docs`. npm workspaces must use those paths (not legacy `client`/`server`).

## Constraints
- Primary user environment is **iPhone** (no assumed always-on PC). Prefer console/mobile-friendly steps; do not require Windows-only tooling as the only path.
- Do not commit secrets (DuckDNS token, SSH keys under `90_secret/`, JWT/DB passwords).
- Live HTTP mockup: `sumicchogurashi.duckdns.org` → `129.225.196.226`. HTTPS may still be pending.
- Local auth without Postgres: `MEMORY_AUTH=1`. Auth is wired in the client; assets/subscriptions/etc. may still be mock data.

## After coding
- Update `10_docs/작업내용.md` (checkboxes, blockers, next steps, date).
- Keep changes scoped; put deep design in dedicated docs (`DB_스키마.md`, `인증_가족_API.md`, infra checklist).
- Cross-tool baseline also lives in root `AGENTS.md` — keep it consistent when instructions change.
